"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoodpecker=self.webpackChunkwoodpecker||[]).push([["9006"],{76919(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"name":"Bluesky Post","slug":"bluesky-post","url":"https://codeberg.org/woodpecker-plugins/bluesky-post","icon":"https://codeberg.org/woodpecker-plugins/bluesky-post/raw/branch/main/bluesky.svg","description":"Post statuses to Bluesky.","docs":"<h1>Bluesky Post plugin</h1>\\n<p>Woodpecker plugin to post statuses to Bluesky.</p>\\n<h2>Usage</h2>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">image: woodpeckerci/plugin-bluesky-post\\nsettings:\\n  identifier: woodpecker-ci.org\\n  app_password:\\n    from_secret: bluesky_app_password\\n  text: We just released {{ CI_COMMIT_TAG }} \u{1F680}\\n</code></pre>\\n<h3>Settings</h3>\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Setting</th>\\n<th>Description</th>\\n<th>Required?</th>\\n<th>Default</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody><tr>\\n<td><code>service_url</code></td>\\n<td>Bluesky service url, including protocol.</td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td><a href=\\"https://bsky.social\\">https://bsky.social</a></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>identifier</code></td>\\n<td>Your Bluesky handle (without @) or did</td>\\n<td>Yes</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>app_password</code></td>\\n<td>Your Bluesky app password (<a href=\\"#get-app-password\\">How to get an app password</a>)</td>\\n<td>Yes</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>text</code></td>\\n<td>Text to post (Allows <a href=\\"#templating\\">Templating</a> and auto detects facets)</td>\\n<td>Yes (if <code>ai_token</code> is not set)</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>files</code></td>\\n<td><code>,</code>-separated paths or globs of images or a video, see <a href=\\"#media\\">Media</a></td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>media</code></td>\\n<td><code>{ path, alt, captions }</code> list, instead of <code>files</code>, see <a href=\\"#media\\">Media</a></td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>languages</code></td>\\n<td><code>,</code>-separated <a href=\\"https://atproto.com/specs/lexicon#language\\">language codes</a> (max 3), e.g. <code>en</code> not <code>english</code></td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>tags</code></td>\\n<td><code>,</code>-separated list of post tags</td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_token</code></td>\\n<td>Provide an AI token (OpenAI) to generate a post text</td>\\n<td>Yes (if <code>text</code> is not set)</td>\\n<td></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_model</code></td>\\n<td>Select the model used to generate a post text</td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td><code>gpt-5-nano</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_url</code></td>\\n<td>Base URL of an OpenAI compatible API, e.g. <a href=\\"#self-hosted-models\\">Ollama</a></td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td>OpenAI</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>ai_prompt</code></td>\\n<td>Prompt used to generate a post text. (Allows <a href=\\"#templating\\">Templating</a>)</td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td><a href=\\"#default-ai-prompt\\">prompt</a></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>changelog_file</code></td>\\n<td>File to use for the AI to make a changelog from.</td>\\n<td>No</td>\\n<td><code>CHANGELOG.md</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table>\\n<h3>Media</h3>\\n<p>A post can have either up to 4 JPEG, PNG, GIF or WebP images of at most 2 MB each, or one MP4 video of at most 300 MB.</p>\\n<p><code>files</code> takes paths or globs like <code>dist/*.png</code>, and the path of each file is used as its alt text.</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">settings:\\n  files:\\n    - dist/screenshot.png\\n    - docs/release/*.png\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>To set your own alt texts, use <code>media</code> instead of <code>files</code>. Each entry needs a <code>path</code>, globs are not supported. The <code>alt</code>\\ntext allows <a href=\\"#templating\\">Templating</a>, and without it the path is used. Set <code>alt: \\"\\"</code> for purely decorative images.\\nA video can have up to 20 WebVTT <code>captions</code> of at most 20 kB each, every one with a <a href=\\"https://atproto.com/specs/lexicon#language\\">BCP 47</a> language tag.</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">settings:\\n  media:\\n    - path: dist/screenshot.png\\n      alt: The new dashboard, released in {{ CI_COMMIT_TAG }}\\n    - path: dist/logo.png\\n      alt: \'\'\\n</code></pre>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">settings:\\n  media:\\n    - path: dist/demo.mp4\\n      alt: A 30 second tour of the new dashboard\\n      captions:\\n        - lang: en\\n          path: dist/demo.en.vtt\\n        - lang: de\\n          path: dist/demo.de.vtt\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>Videos are uploaded through the Bluesky video service, which processes them before the post is created. Bluesky-hosted\\naccounts need a verified email address to upload videos, and the number of videos per day is limited.</p>\\n<p>All files are checked before anything is posted, and every problem is reported at once.</p>\\n<h3>Get app password</h3>\\n<p>In order to get an app password, go to <a href=\\"https://bsky.app/settings/app-passwords\\">https://bsky.app/settings/app-passwords</a> and create a new app password.</p>\\n<h3>Templating</h3>\\n<p>You can use <code>{{ CI_COMMIT_TAG }}</code> and other environment variables in the <code>text</code> or <code>ai_prompt</code> settings.\\nThe <code>ai_prompt</code> template can also use <code>{{ CHANGELOG }}</code> to include the changelog of the release.\\nThe <code>app_password</code> and <code>ai_token</code> values are never available as placeholders, and AI generated text is posted as is.</p>\\n<h3>Self-hosted models</h3>\\n<p>Any server with an OpenAI compatible <code>chat/completions</code> endpoint works, for example <a href=\\"https://ollama.com\\">Ollama</a>.\\n<code>ai_token</code> still enables the AI and is sent as bearer token; a local Ollama ignores it, so any value will do.</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">image: woodpeckerci/plugin-bluesky-post\\nsettings:\\n  identifier: woodpecker-ci.org\\n  app_password:\\n    from_secret: bluesky_app_password\\n  ai_url: http://ollama:11434/v1\\n  ai_token: unused\\n  ai_model: llama3.2\\n</code></pre>\\n<h3>Default AI prompt</h3>\\n<p>Used when <code>ai_prompt</code> is not set. Copy of the prompt defined in <a href=\\"https://codeberg.org/woodpecker-plugins/bluesky-post/src/branch/main/src/utils.ts\\"><code>src/utils.ts</code></a>:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-text\\">We want to announce the next version of our app on Bluesky.\\nWrite a catchy post, so users will know why they should update to the newest\\nversion. If there is no special feature included, just summarize the changes\\nin a few sentences. Reply with the post text only, at most 300 characters long.\\n\\nThe changelog entry: {{ changelog }}\\n</code></pre>\\n","tags":["post","status","bluesky"],"containerImage":"woodpeckerci/plugin-bluesky-post","containerImageUrl":"https://hub.docker.com/r/woodpeckerci/plugin-bluesky-post","verified":true,"iconDataUrl":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,"}')}}]);